<h2 id="describe-your-app">3. Describe your app</h2>

<p>
  Tell Copilot what you want to make in your local session and ask it to use
  <code>hyb26-skill</code>. The prompt below is only an example. You do not need
  to copy it or use it as written; describe your own idea in your own words.
</p>

<CopyPrompt prompt="Use hyb26-skill to make a badge app with a counter that increases when I press SELECT. Walk me through anything I need to do with the badge using plain English." />

<p>
  Answer Copilot's questions. If a permission request appears, check that it is
  for your local project, the installed skill tools, or BADGER before allowing
  it. You may still need to approve a tool action; the prompt does not bypass
  those controls. Do not use an allow-everything option.
</p>

<p>
  On macOS, your tool may also ask for access to Documents or removable volumes.
  Allow only access needed for this work; do not grant broad disk access or
  disable safety settings.
</p>

<p>
  Copilot should check the app before copying it. If the skill, Python, or badge
  tools are missing, or Copilot cannot identify the badge, ask staff for help
  rather than skip the checks.
</p>
